From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:50:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST: flag StaleWarPeace (end wars that are going
 nowhere)

Bully pair 0879B791: the Celts declared on the Netherlands at T111, their
siege failed by T116 (11 units lost), and the war ran to T150. The beaten
Celts were willing to make peace from T116 on (peace score up to 129); the
Netherlands refused every turn (-11 to -67): CP's "they're in danger and
we're not, hold out" term, multiplied up to 5x against a PATHETIC enemy,
outweighed the progress penalty. But the Netherlands never attacked
(war state Calm, no captures), so the leverage it held out for never
turned into anything.

With the flag, a war is stale after 20+ turns with no city changing hands
in either direction for 20 turns and no attack operation of ours against
them. Then: staleness is reason enough to consider peace, the hold-out
term for their danger is dropped, and the lack-of-progress penalty counts
twice. A winner that presses its attack is unaffected.

Off in the bundle until tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj1hm6um5X9SZaXQCRZ
